message.content:
{"diagnosis": "Trace shows `TRAP: no progress max_addr=0x00000000` and `tohost: FAIL 0xdead` after 2009 cycles, meaning PC never advanced through 256-word NOP mem where progress was expected. CONE_SLICE is empty so trace wins. Root cause is picorv32.v:1450 `do_waitirq <= 1;` as the every-cycle default, which forces WFI stall and blocks fetch; it should be 0 and asserted only on WFI.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -1448,8 +1448,8 @@
 		decoder_pseudo_trigger <= 0;
 		decoder_pseudo_trigger_q <= decoder_pseudo_trigger;
-		do_waitirq <= 1;
+		do_waitirq <= 0;

 		trace_valid <= 0;

 		if (!ENABLE_TRACE)
 			trace_data <= 'bx;
", "expected": "tohost PASS with progress max_addr != 0x00000000, no TRAP: no progress, no FAIL 0xdead"}

